{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>A day or two days.</b> A day, which is like days, meaning from time to time (a full twenty-four hours). For one cannot say literally two days, since if for one day he is exempt, for two days all the more so. And according to its plain sense, the way of Scripture is to say thus: this case, and all the more so that one — as in 'on the word of two witnesses or three witnesses.'" "<b>For he is his money.</b> And it is in his hand to strike him, but only by way of reproof."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:59:25.985331909Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}